        <type>STDMETHOD</type>
        <definition>STDMETHOD debug::EventCallbacks::GetInterestMask</definition>
        <argsstring>(PULONG mask) override</argsstring>
        <name>GetInterestMask</name>
        <qualifiedname>debug::EventCallbacks::GetInterestMask</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>PULONG</type>
          <declname>mask</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Report which event categories this callback is interested in. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Sets the mask to breakpoints, exceptions, process creation and exit, and module load. Every other IDebugEventCallbacks method is a required override of the COM interface that dbgeng never invokes, because its event bit is not in this mask.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>mask</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Receives the interest mask bitmask (DEBUG_EVENT_*). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>S_OK always. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
