        <briefdescription>
<para>Called when a DLL or EXE is loaded into the target. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Stops the target so the main loop can resolve pending breakpoints against the new module. While a step is pending the method records nothing and returns DEBUG_STATUS_NO_CHANGE. Otherwise it sets stopReason to moduleLoad and records the image name in <ref refid="classdebug_1_1_state_1a3de08ce6e5b86e52f6e9fc2644f3d0f1" kindref="member">State::lastLoadedImageName</ref>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>imageFileHandle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Handle to the module image file. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>baseOffset</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Base load address of the module. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>moduleSize</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Size of the module image. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>moduleName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Short module name. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>imageName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Full path to the module image file. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>checkSum</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>PE checksum of the module. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>timeDateStamp</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>PE timestamp of the module. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>DEBUG_STATUS_BREAK when the module load stops the target, otherwise DEBUG_STATUS_NO_CHANGE. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
